Z||000000||Ferrari_cdn||08-23-2001||10:08 PM||||Ok well I found out that for some reason the sunroof in the 84SE is sealed shut and if I want to use it I would have to get rubber moldings or some sort.  Is this easy/cheap repair to do?  What should I expect if I will replace that?||||reg||1
Z||000001||baldlobo||08-23-2001||10:47 PM||||there is a guy on henderson who can help you with any parts you need, Mach should know his number(I'm feeling lazey right now or else I would try and find his number for you)  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000002||DecadenceR||08-24-2001||01:49 AM||||If you eman the rubber seal that goes around the roof, it costs about $60 from the fiero store, and I think it took me 20 minutes to rip out the old one and install the new one.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Monkeyman||08-25-2001||06:01 AM||||Are you sure it's actually sealed shut and not just sticking to the weatherstrip?||||reg||1
Z||000004||Tina||08-25-2001||12:34 PM||||<BR>Just an idea.<BR>Not really familiar with sunroofs, but could<BR>it be the previous owner sealed the sunroof shut on purpose?<BR>Happend to me with my t-tops.<P>Tina  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000005||theogre||08-25-2001||01:19 PM||||From what I've seen. the 84 roof is slightly different from the later years. the newer ones have a "paint" around the edge that provides a boarder area on the panel. The 84's don't have that boarder. The seal could be simply stuck to the glass, or as Tina mentioned, it could be glued.<P>If it's glued, there should be signs of it along the seal/glass joint. No one ever gets glue perfect.<P>If you can't find signs of adhesive. Try sraying a little water on the top and along the inside of the seal with an old spray bottle. Try working a plastic padle like what is used for spreading body filler between the glass and seal from the inside. The water may help you get in there better. The plastic shouldn't hurt the seal like metal would.||||reg||1
